00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:06.280 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  happy Diwali to all my Indian fans so a  lot of you have been requesting for  another healthy India meal plan in my  previous India meal plan video I shared  some really simple and useful tips to  cook Indian food without sacrificing the  flavours yet keeping it healthy so do  check it out on my youtube channel  Indian cooking can be complicated and  also time-consuming so I'm recreating  some of my favourite recipes which are  really simple fast and also healthy this  recipes are vegan friendly they are  gluten free and also dairy free so we've  got breakfast lunch and also dinner for  breakfast I'm making my version of a  savory Indian pancakes the ingredients  you need are 1 cup of rice flour 1/3 cup  of red onion diced 1/3 cup of carrot  grater  1 red chili finely chopped about 3  tablespoons of coriander finely chopped  1/2 a tbsp of vegetable oil  approximately 1/3 cup of warm water in a  bowl mix in the rice flour onions  carrots coriander chilies combined well  then add in the water little by little  to make the dough if it's too thick then  add in more water grease a nonstick pan  with oil over medium low heat  pull the batter equally onto the pan to  cook the pancakes this should make about  6 pancakes guys don't worry if your  pancakes do not look perfect cook for  about 3 to 4 minutes on one side until  it is slightly brown then flip over and  continue to cook until the pancakes are  done serve warm instead of the sugar  loaded sweet pancakes these pancakes are  filled with vegetables so each pancake  has about 120 calories so have three to  four pancakes for breakfast to fill your  body and  the energy you need for the day for  lunch I'm making rice noodle upma this  recipe is great because you can prep  ahead and bring it out to work or school  what you'll need are three ounces of  rice noodles one small onion diced one  red chili finely chopped one sprig of  curry leaves 1 tablespoon of vegetable  oil 1 tablespoon of chana dal half a  teaspoon of cumin quarter teaspoon of  black mustard seeds cut a cup of cashew  nuts haft 3/4 cup of mixed carrots corn  and peas  let's start by prepping the noodles  stock noodles in boiling water for about  5 minutes or until soft then drain and  set aside in a non-stick pan heat oil  over medium high heat add in the cumin  black mustard seeds and Dow fry very  quickly for about 3 to 4 minutes until  the Daltons slightly golden and fragrant  then stir in curry leaves chili mixed  vegetables The Onion's cashew nuts saute  very quickly for another two to three  minutes and two cashews are slightly  roasted finally mix in the noodles and  stir until all the ingredients are  evenly distributed at this point you can  go ahead and taste your dish add more  salt if needed garnish with a little bit  of coriander and serve warm so this is  my take on rice noodle upma which is  more like a stir-fried noodle dish it is  easy quick and very convenient to be  eaten each serving has about 370  calories if you want to you can even mix  a protein into the dish such as meat  fish tempeh or even tofu this is your  dish to experiment with as for dinner  I'll be serving chickpeas sweet potato  greens in coconut milk why you'll need  are 1 medium onion diced 1 garlic clove  peeled 1 ginger piece thumb-sized peeled  and sliced  one red chilli finely sliced half a  tablespoon of vegetable oil  half a teaspoon of turmeric powder 1  teaspoon of cumin powder 1 teaspoon of  garam masala 2 cups of pumpkin peeled  and diced one can of chickpeas rinsed  and drained about 150 grams of sweet  potato greens one cup of coconut milk 1  cup of vegetable stock let's start by  prepping the paste in a food processor  add in the onion ginger garlic and  chilli blend very quickly until it  becomes a paste in a large nonstick pan  heat oil over medium high heat fry the  paste very quickly for one to two  minutes until fragrant and then add in  the spices turmeric cumin and garam  masala continue to fry very quickly for  another minute next add chickpeas and  pumpkin stir and mix well then add in  vegetable stock the coconut milk and  bring to a simmer and allow all the  ingredients to cook for about 20 to 30  minutes until the pumpkin softens and  the sauce thickens don't forget to stir  occasionally  so once the pumpkin has softened then  add in the sweet potato greens and cook  until wilted serve warm I just love the  nutty and earthy flavor of chickpeas  combined with the sweetness of pumpkin  and also the creaminess of coconut milk  this dish is just bursting with flavors  and it is so delicious so one serving  has about 267 calories you can serve  this with a cup of rice or 2 chapatis I  hope you loved all these recipes I like  to keep it simple balanced and moderate  do try this recipes out take pictures  and share them with me at Joanna's  official hashtag the choice of recipes  let me know which is your favorite in  the comments below do also like this  video share this video with your friends  and  subscribe to my youtube channel for a  lot more healthy recipes and workout  videos don't forget to turn on your  notification button so that you will get  notified every time I share a new video  happy Diwali

